Tuesday Update
* Sold half of new CI calls for big gain; ORCL calls in gear*&nbsp;Stocks v=
olatile as Fed chief testifies in Congress&nbsp;Stocks pared losses Tuesday=
 but technology remained among the worst performers after Federal Reserve C=
hairman Jerome Powell told Congress that the economy was a "long way from o=
ur employment and inflation goals."The Dow Jones Industrial Average fell by=
 129.60 points, or 0.4%, to 31,392 after retreating to as low as 31,250 ear=
lier in the session. S&amp;P 500 slid by 0.7% to 3,847.00 and Nasdaq droppe=
d by 1.9% to 13,274.55, but both indexes were off their session lows. Consu=
mer discretionary was the steepest decliner while energy led the gainers af=
ter midday on Tuesday.The US 10-year yield fell by 1.9 basis points to just=
 under 1.35%, after earlier trading higher at 1.37%. The West Texas Interme=
diate futures fell by 0.1% to $61.62, recovering from declines of as much a=
s 0.8%.The current monetary policy stance remains appropriate and it will b=
e "some time" before any changes are required, Powell was cited as saying i=
n a comment from Pantheon Macroeconomics on Tuesday."Inflation is no near-t=
erm threat, thanks to the impact of COVID on some sector, but the Chair rem=
inded Senators that even when inflation does rise, the Fed wants to see it =
above the target for 'some time' before raising rates," Powell was cited as=
 saying in the Pantheon commentary.In company news, Extra Space Storage (EX=
R) reported fourth-quarter results that beat expectations and the company s=
et upbeat earnings guidance while raising its quarterly dividend. Shares ju=
mped by 6.2% intraday, the most on S&amp;P 500.Home Depot (HD) said net ear=
nings in the fourth quarter were affected by expenses from its acquisition =
of HD Supply in December, which totaled $0.09 a share. Shares fell by 4.6%,=
 the most on the Dow, even as the company reported higher sales and earning=
s than the market had anticipated.Portfolio: We bought CI calls Monday and =
already sold half for a 37% gain; adjust second target and stop=E2=80=A6 We=
 bought ORCL calls and they are higher; adjust target/stop.&nbsp; ... No ne=
w recommendations.*CURRENT RECOMMENDATIONSCIGNA Corp. (CI) March 210 calls-=
- Symbol: CI210319C00210000-- Bought at $5.90 on Feb 22-- Sold half today F=
eb 23 at $8.10 for a 37.3.% gain!-- Now trading at $9.25-- Set up to sell t=
he rest at new $10.15-- Set stop at new $6.00 good after 10:30 a.m. ET only=
*Oracle Corp. (ORCL) March 60 calls-- Symbol: ORCL210319C00060000-- Bought =
at $5.15 on Feb 22-- Now trading at $5.55-- Sell half at $6.70 lmt gtc and =
half at $8.0 lmt gtc-- Set stop at new $4.10 stp, good after 10:30 a.m. ET =
only*Thanks for reading,Jon D. MarkmanAll recommendations are for monthly o=
ptions expiring on the third Friday of the specified month unless otherwise=
 noted. All stops are good after 10:30 a.m. Eastern only unless otherwise s=
pecified. All orders are good for the day only unless otherwise noted. "Day=
 only" orders expire at the close of the current session. Past results are =
no guarantee of future returns. All accounts may not achieve comparable res=
ults. Recommendations are leveraged and speculative, so only use risk capit=
al =E2=80=94 i.e., money you can afford to lose. All results are shown ex-c=
ommissions and fees. Options trading involves the risk of substantial loss.=
